          "update_time": 1794182774.781,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "**B04 is complete. It identified a precise limitation of the averaging route and a concrete next calculation.**\n\nThe main analytical result is that one hypothetical off-line zero at transverse distance \\(d\\) contributes total Green mass \\(\\pi d\\). Averaging over a height interval of length \\(T\\) dilutes its signal to at most \\(\\pi d/T\\). Applying the [inherited zero-density estimate](https://arxiv.org/html/1404.3080v2) gives an upper allowance that stays of constant size. That particular averaging argument therefore cannot resolve a single exceptional zero.\n\nThis explains why better statistical information can coexist with an unresolved exclusion problem. The limitation concerns the stated averaging bound; sharper local arithmetic estimates remain possible. The derivation and its scope are in the [research note](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-5/08_theta_observables_newman_dynamics/03_operator_imaginary_time_evolution/01_green_potential_resolvent/notes/09_TND_OG_B04_GREEN_MASS_RESOLUTION_AND_VALUE_DECISION_20261108.md), currently checked by the proof author only.\n\nThe computational alternative now has a useful first question: **can the existing acquisition proof support a practical calculation?** E03 guarantees arbitrary accuracy, but its logarithmic and integration bounds may demand substantial work. I prepared one fixed, low-height calibration task to calculate the prescribed panel count and error requirements before building an evaluator. No numerical run or favorable signed value is claimed.\n\n**Next: [E] TND-OG-E06 — Sol6.1**, the bounded feasibility check. Its possible outcomes determine whether to prepare an implementation or first improve the estimates.\n\nProgress, notes, the self-check and chat history are recorded. The [continuation and model-change note](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-5/08_theta_observables_newman_dynamics/03_operator_imaginary_time_evolution/01_green_potential_resolvent/continuation-notes/11_TND_OG_B04_RESULTS_AND_MODEL_CHANGE_20261108.md) contains the execution prompt and stopping rules."
            ]
          },
